"src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":145,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":79815356155260,"name":"RYM Top — Singer-Songwriter — Canzone d'autore","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":145,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":149265815440484,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Punk Poetry","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":145,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":154109104558245,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Gipsy Punk","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":145,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":184428705628870,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Folk Punk","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":145,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":196140923370937,"name":"RYM Top — Experimental — Tape Music","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":145,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":201357142129870,"name":"RYM Top — Folk — Sa'idi","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":145,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":235913166157674,"name":"RYM Top — Electronic — Hard Dance","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":145,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":265496132631976,"name":"RYM Top — Hip Hop — Gangstarap","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":145,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":44735175437010,"name":"AOTY Must Hear 2000s","src":"charts","grp":"AOTY","list_year":null,"rank":393,"year":2002,"note":null,"total":520,"scaruffi":null}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"Released in 2002, this album was one of three strong albums that contributed to Queens of the Stone Age becoming a serious force. \"three strong albums, rated R in 2000, Songs For The Death in 2002, and Lilabai's to Paralyze in 2005.\"","year":2002,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 00's Part 3: The Return of Rock","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7dXtgTkdv9w"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"Released in the summer of 2002, this album was conceived as a concept record, though its conceptual nature is subtle and often missed. It is intended to be a soundtrack for a drive from Los Angeles through the desert to Joshua Tree National Park, with the listener flipping through small-town radio stations along the way. The artwork on some versions of the album depicts the dashboard of a Fiat 124 spider, visually representing this journey. \"This is supposed to be taken as a soundtrack of a drive from Los Angeles through to Joshua Tree National Park out in the desert, while flipping through small town radio stations along the way, hence the dashboard of a Fiat 124 spider shown in the artwork of some versions of the album.\"","year":2002,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Alt Rock Concept Albums: Part 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1KyNY3zv6uc"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This album was recorded with Josh Homme, Nic Oliveri, and Mark Lanegan, and featured Dave Grohl as a full-time drummer who joined halfway through the sessions. The record incorporated interstitial bits with fake radio DJs to simulate listening to a car radio driving in the desert at night, where every station change would play a Queens of the Stone Age song. Despite the concept, the record label reportedly disliked the album from the demo stage. The title was inspired by the band's sound engineer, who played music at dance parties for deaf people, where attendees enjoyed feeling the bass by holding large balloons. \"The audience loved it when he pumped up the bass, which they could really feel by holding big balloons.\"","year":2002,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Secrets of Queens of the Stone Age: Part 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BvhjsTUIS2o"}]}],"book_tracks":[],"others":[{"id":152910294857286,"type":"album","name":"Rated R","year":2000,"weight":39},{"id":223355448440185,"type":"album","name":"...Like Clockwork","year":2013,"weight":29},{"id":194059298112688,"type":"album","name":"Villains","year":2017,"weight":25},{"id":29600814638964,"type":"album","name":"Queens of the Stone Age","year":1998,"weight":23},{"id":218576463867867,"type":"album","name":"Lullabies to Paralyze","year":2005,"weight":16},{"id":111404380488563,"type":"song","name":"No One Knows","year":2002,"weight":15},{"id":99811088538300,"type":"song","name":"The Way You Used to Do","year":2017,"weight":12},{"id":1543760395018,"type":"song","name":"My God Is the Sun","year":2013,"weight":12},{"id":150212437414342,"type":"song","name":"Little Sister","year":2005,"weight":9},{"id":57800811597490,"type":"album","name":"In Times New Roman…","year":2023,"weight":9},{"id":46244373107145,"type":"song","name":"Go with the Flow","year":2002,"weight":9},{"id":264857950822519,"type":"album","name":"Era Vulgaris","year":2007,"weight":7}]}